  "body": "## What\n\nDeepSeek-V4.1-Flash on SM120 now uses the numerics of DeepSeek's reference `inference/` code in two places where the gain costs no speed.\n\n1. **Sparse attention runs in BF16.** The b12x V4.1 tuner could pick FP8 internals: Q and P quantized, KV re-encoded to FP8. On the current beta it did so for all prefill plans and most decode plans. That was about 3.4% relative error (cosine 0.9994) against the reference `sparse_attn` (BF16 Q, KV dequantized to BF16, BF16 P, FP32 accumulation). The BF16 plans are 0.3% (split-K decode) and 5e-5 (single-pass).\n   - `VLLM_DS41_ATTENTION_COMPUTE` selects the mode:\n     - `bf16` (default);\n     - `reference`: decode rows also run single-pass, which reproduces the reference kernel's tile-ordered softmax bit for bit;\n     - `auto`: the previous tuner choice.\n2. **Logits are FP32.** The reference head computes FP32 logits. vLLM's BF16 head rounded them to steps of up to 1/8: every logprob gap in the dumps sat on the 1/32 grid.\n   - On SM120 the DS4.1 target and DSpark draft now default to `head_dtype=float32` (`torch.mm(..., out_dtype=float32)`).\n   - `--hf-overrides '{\"head_dtype\": \"model\"}'` restores BF16.\n   - `head_dtype=float32` used to raise for runtime-quantized LM heads, so it could not run with the optional NVFP4 DSpark drafter and Markov heads (`VLLM_DS41_DRAFT_NVFP4_HEAD`, `VLLM_DS41_MARKOV_NVFP4`). Those heads now keep their kernel and have their logits widened.\n\nThe companion b12x change (local-inference-lab/b12x#435, merged) makes the 288-byte FP4 compressed KV records bit-identical to the reference quantizer.\n\n## Measurements (4x RTX PRO 6000, TP4, ds41-flash profile)\n\n**Accuracy against the reference.** DeepSeek's reference `model.py` was run TP4 on the same token ids.\n- Attention kernel alone (16 heads, 128 window + 512 compressed keys, sink):\n\n  | Mode | Relative error | Bit-identical BF16 outputs |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | FP8 (tuner default) | 3.4e-2 | 5% |\n  | BF16 split-K | 3e-3 | ~50% |\n  | BF16 single-pass (`reference`) | 5e-5 | ~100% |\n\n- End to end, KL(reference \u2016 vLLM) over 49k document positions:\n  - 0.0084 for the beta and for every variant of this change;\n  - injecting any single BF16/FP8-level difference into the reference already produces ~0.0075, so the whole stack sits at the numerical-noise floor;\n  - BF16 logits alone contribute 0.00023 and flip the argmax at 0.44% of positions.\n- Task accuracy, DSpark off:\n  - GSM8K (1319, greedy): 96.66% / 96.97% vs beta 96.74%;\n  - needles 32k/64k/128k: 100%;\n  - NLL over 131k-token books: within noise.\n\n**Speed.** DSpark is on (profile default, probabilistic drafts, standard rejection sampling). Mixed reasoning/essay/code requests, 512 tokens, two repetitions:\n\n| | C1 tok/s | C8 tok/s | C32 tok/s | accepted / draft |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| beta | 233\u2013236 | 660\u2013667 | 1340\u20131357 | 1.81\u20131.83 |\n| this PR (defaults) | 231\u2013239 | 666\u2013667 | 1338\u20131362 | 1.77\u20131.83 |\n| this PR + NVFP4 drafter/Markov heads | 233\u2013239 | 666 | 1347\u20131350 | 1.76\u20131.81 |\n\n- DSpark acceptance per workload (GSM8K with thinking, essays, code) is unchanged: 1.745\u20131.768 tokens per draft across all variants, 1.748 on beta.\n- Greedy GSM8K-200 with DSpark: 97\u201399% in every variant.\n- DSpark off, bf16 split-K vs beta: 131/630/1325/94 vs 133/620/1326/95 tok/s at C1/C8/C32/C1@16k.\n- `reference` mode costs 9% at C1 and 17% at C1 with 16k context.\n- FP32 logits are confirmed in the served logprobs: 0/456 top-20 gaps on the BF16 grid, vs 456/456 on beta.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/quantization/test_lm_head.py::test_fp32_head_dtype_widens_quantized_head_logits` (new).\n- The rest of `test_lm_head.py` is unchanged: 3 tests fail identically on the unmodified beta image (test fixture lacks `online_quantization_config`).\n- b12x V4.1 writer and attention tests: 70 passed with #435.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
